===persian===

باران،
تو از آسمان بازمی‌گردی
تا قصهٔ دلتنگی خود را
برای خاک بگویی...
اما بوی کاهگل... مَجال شکوه نمی‌دهد...
زمستان ۱۳۶۸

===machine===

Rain,
you come back down from the sky
to tell the earth
the story of your own longing...
but the smell of straw-and-clay... leaves no room for complaint...
Winter 1368

===lantern===

Rain,
you come back down out of the sky
to tell the earth
the story of your own homesickness...
but the smell of adobe... gives you no opening to complain...

Winter 1368

===translation===

===footnotes===

Five lines and a complete reversal: the rain descends in order to complain, and
what its own arrival releases from the ground — the smell of wet adobe — leaves it nothing to
complain about. مجال is the room or opening to do a thing, so the rain is not refuted, it is simply
given no gap to speak into.

